<blockquote class="uncited"><div>While I read the User Guide (thank you), let me ask:<br><br>It seems to me that the RD-5R is missing two important features of the GD-77, so as to not bastardize sales of the GD-77:<br><br>1) An ability to program a new DMR repeater from the keyboard (requiring use of a computer even "on the road"); and<br><br>2) A very limited memory to hold Digital Contacts, such as the hundreds of thousands of worldwide Digital IDs.<br><br>Does the Open version of the firmware fix these two deficiencies?<br><br>Also, what do you mean by "grapped?"</div></blockquote>The OpenGD77 firmware is completely different to the official firmware on any of these radios.<br>The OpenGD77/DM1801/RD5R does not have a lot of the features that are in the official firmware.<br>SMS is not supported, nor is DCDM and various other things.<br><br>Your guess is as good as mine to why various features are not in the official RD5R firmware, but ultimately the firmware for all these radios is written by the same secretive organistion, whose name we can't determine. <br><br>The OpenRD5R is most of the features of the OpenGD77/ OpenDM108, except for Hotspot mode, and some features in the future can't be supported on the RD-5R due to hardware limitations.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Mon Aug 23, 2021 2:53 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
