		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=827&amp;p=13958#p13958"><![CDATA[
The firmware loader uses different protocol than CPS, so it doesn't want COM port, it's happy with HID device. So you can use tha cable which you have and if you start the radio in bootloader mode, it will find it and flash it. I'm using a separate flasher available for GD-77, possibly the same will work for BF-5R, but you can start the flash from CPS, it will work as well, even if CPS itself doesn't communicate.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=958">ok1pt</a> — Wed Mar 17, 2021 4:32 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
